{
  "self": "Low-key online socializer; prefers small, slow, text-heavy communities over algorithm-driven feeds and misses old internet forum culture: familiar usernames, signatures, slow conversations. Lurker by default, regular in retro gaming/art/music servers. Values being part of a room's texture rather than its focus; saves little, likes finite sharing. Winds down with lo-fi, ambient, post-rock, and game soundtracks: Chrono Trigger, EarthBound, Ocarina of Time, Animal Crossing hourly themes, Minecraft Volume Beta, Skyrim Secunda/Far Horizons. Loves AC 5PM GameCube, 1AM rainy, New Leaf 7PM; grey skies, actual or simulated rain, rainy-night mixes with distant cars. Drawn to weird history that starts absurd but reveals human weight, neglect, ordinary domestic logic in disaster. Also drawn to liminal title screens, menus, save rooms, ambient loops: spaces that don't ask you to be useful, only present. PS2 black-blue void feels like an abandoned observatory; GameCube startup is an entrance, PS2 is already inside. Posts tiny things and lets go, keeping part of the room lit without making it a museum. Keeps a tiny text file of signature/status lines as a tide mark, not a collection; current line often 'title screen, cup going cold, not saving,' changing only when it no longer feels like mine. Recently tends to phrase the room as weather, not status.",
  "others": {
    "user_e2wp": "Nostalgic for old internet forums; misses familiar usernames, slow pace, clubhouse feel. Thinks mainstream too fast; values intentionality and small hobby Discords with same thirty people daily. Reads old threads for signature texture; loved 'I put the pro in procrastinate.' Keeps notes file of signature/status phrases, just line and year, no thread. Prefers old permanent signatures over rotating statuses. Lines include 'quiet, rain on window, no respawns,' 'loading screen, fan on, summer without updates,' stray 'empty server, cursor slow, frag limit off.'",
